    "cursorSync": "Crosshair",
    "description": "Australia’s largest power station in 3D on its satellite image, each of its four 720 MW units in the colour of what it is doing now, from AEMO’s five-minute SCADA readings, with the station’s output, each unit’s output and what each did over the day.",
    "editable": true,
    "elements": {
      "panel-1": {
        "kind": "Panel",
        "spec": {
          "data": {
            "kind": "QueryGroup",
            "spec": {
              "queries": [],
              "queryOptions": {},
              "transformations": []
            }
          },
          "description": "",
          "id": 1,
          "links": [],
          "title": "What you are looking at",
          "vizConfig": {
            "group": "text",
            "kind": "VizConfig",
            "spec": {
              "fieldConfig": {
                "defaults": {},
                "overrides": []
              },
              "options": {
                "code": {
                  "language": "plaintext",
                  "showLineNumbers": false,
                  "showMiniMap": false
                },
                "content": "Eraring Power Station on Lake Macquarie, New South Wales: Australia's largest power station, four coal-fired units of 720 MW, due to close in 2027. Each unit's output as AEMO's SCADA reads it, every five minutes, as the market's operator publishes it for every generator on the grid; the recorder keeps a week of it. On the map the station stands on its satellite image in 3D, each unit in the colour of what it is doing now: off, at low load (under half of 720 MW), running, or at full load (90 % and more). Around midday Eraring often turns down, or stops units, while rooftop and utility solar cover the demand. Tilt and turn the map with the right button or Ctrl+drag; hover a unit for its reading.\n\nData: [AEMO NEMweb](https://nemweb.com.au/Reports/Current/Dispatch_SCADA/), dispatch SCADA, five-minute intervals in market time (AEST, UTC+10), used under AEMO's copyright permissions. The model is a schematic drawn on the station's footprint in OpenStreetMap (via Overture Maps, ODbL): which end of the block is unit 1, the houses' heights and where the two chimneys stand are not surveyed.",
                "mode": "markdown"
              }
            },
            "version": "13.2.1"
          }
        }
      },
      "panel-2": {
        "kind": "Panel",
        "spec": {
          "data": {
            "kind": "QueryGroup",
            "spec": {
              "queries": [
                {
                  "kind": "PanelQuery",
                  "spec": {
                    "hidden": false,
                    "query": {
                      "datasource": {
                        "name": "duckdb"
                      },
                      "group": "motherduck-duckdb-datasource",
                      "kind": "DataQuery",
                      "spec": {
                        "format": 1,
                        "rawQuery": true,
                        "rawSql": "-- The station's latest reading: its output, the share of its 2,880 MW, the\n-- units running, and how old the reading is (AEMO publishes every five\n-- minutes; over a quarter of an hour means the recorder or AEMO is late).\nWITH latest AS (\n  SELECT duid, arg_max(mw, ts) AS mw, max(ts) AS ts\n  FROM read_parquet([${files:singlequote}])\n  WHERE duid IN ('ER01', 'ER02', 'ER03', 'ER04')\n  GROUP BY duid\n)\nSELECT round(sum(greatest(mw, 0))) AS \"Output (MW)\",\n       round(100 * sum(greatest(mw, 0)) / 2880) AS \"Of capacity\",\n       count(*) FILTER (WHERE mw \u003e= 10) || ' of 4' AS \"Units running\",\n       -- AEMO stamps a reading with the end of its five-minute interval and\n       -- publishes it before that end: the age runs from the interval's start.\n       greatest(round(date_diff('second', max(ts) - INTERVAL 5 MINUTE, now()) / 60), 0) AS \"Reading age\"\nFROM latest\n"
                      },
                      "version": "v0"
                    },
                    "refId": "A"
                  }
                }
              ],
              "queryOptions": {},
              "transformations": []
            }
          },
          "description": "",
          "id": 2,
          "links": [],
          "title": "The station now",
          "vizConfig": {
            "group": "stat",
            "kind": "VizConfig",
            "spec": {
              "fieldConfig": {
                "defaults": {
                  "color": {
                    "fixedColor": "text",
                    "mode": "fixed"
                  },
                  "decimals": 0
                },
